{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774707,"nonce":"L7qcS8zH84TT9xm7v28cH45BFUc=","title":"ADR-0039: Privileged step images — hardened baseline + governed capability grants per Environment","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #2 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0039-privileged-images` → `feat/adr-0037-environment-governance`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-14T09:12:08Z · Merged: 2026-07-14T09:20:28Z\n\nImplements **ADR-0039** — bucket (d) of the plugins discussion: governing which OCI images may run with elevated privilege, per Environment.\n\n\u003e **Stacked on #1 (ADR-0037).** Base is `feat/adr-0037-environment-governance`; this PR shows only the ADR-0039 diff. Merge #1 first — GitHub will retarget this to `main` automatically.\n\n- **Hardened baseline (the floor)** — every step Pod now gets a k8s \"restricted\"-equivalent `SecurityContext` (runAsNonRoot, drop ALL caps, RuntimeDefault seccomp, allowPrivilegeEscalation:false). Previously normal step pods set **no** security context at all.\n- **Privilege = closed capability vocabulary, not a binary** — `run-as-root` (self-service, sandbox-bound), `add-capabilities` (caps pinned in the whitelist), `privileged` (the blunt escape hatch). `cluster-access` out; `host-*` deferred (`host-network` a provisional hard no).\n- **Request/grant separation of duties** — author *requests* via `security:` on a step (no authority); Environment admin *grants* via a digest-keyed whitelist on `ProtectionRules` (Administer-only). Fail-closed: a rejected request aborts run creation with a diagnostic, never a silent downgrade.\n- **Tiered keying** — `privileged` is **digest-only forever**; low-risk grants may use signatures once ADR-0015 provenance exists; digest-only for all until then (so this ships with zero dependency on unbuilt provenance).\n- **Fork-PR lockout extends to governed grants** (reuses `locked_out`); privileged requires an Environment (inline `POST /runs` is baseline-only by construction).\n\n`scarab-projects` (grant model + `admit_grants`, no migration — JSON blob) · `scarab-pipeline` (`security:` request + validation) · `scarab-engine`/`-executor-k8s` (admitted-grant launch fields + baseline \u0026 application) · `scarab-server` (fail-closed admission on the trigger path).\n\n20 new unit tests; full suite green (185 pass, 4 ignored) vs local Postgres. Pod `SecurityContext` unit-tested; live-cluster round-trip stays `#[ignore]`.\n\nDeliberate deferrals + their demand triggers recorded in `docs/followups.md`. See `docs/adr/0039-privileged-images.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}